Description: RISC3D: GPU drawing for RISC OS programs (prototype)
 RISC OS programs' OpenGL and OpenGL ES, through riscos-mesa's EGL, drawn
 by Linux's graphics driver (the GPU's where there is one): rol-3d,
 Linux's side. RISC OS's side, !RISC3D in !Boot.Resources (the RISC3D
 module with its Linux3D driver), is the PackMan package RISC3D, which
 riscos-harddisc installs and PackMan updates. Frames go
 straight onto the screen where rol-fb has overlays. Debian's Mesa
 (recommended) is what draws; without it programs keep riscos-mesa's
 software rendering.
